Z||000000||Old Lar||09-30-2000||08:55 PM||||Entered  a local car show today and the 87 GT was classified as a 2 seater sports car... I'm thinking egad, I'll be in a show competing with Corvetts.  Not so..<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sportscarclassM.jpg">  <P>It was Porsches, e type Jags with v-12 no less, Mercedes, MG's and the winner of the class was:   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/56tbirdM.jpg">  I can not find fault with this winner.<P>I did get to see the engine drool of my youth<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/62-409engineM.jpg">  <P>See kiddies what you could put into a 1962 Chevy Biscayne and have the best sleeper on the strip.  This one even had the 4 speed on the floor .<p>[This message has been edited by Old Lar (edited 09-30-2000).]||||reg||8
Z||000001||sluppy123||09-30-2000||09:25 PM||||Looks like all the car shows I enter my GT in. I've been stuck with some very stiff competition (Porsche's, Vette's, BMW's, Lotus, Panteras, ect...) So Far I've placed in every show I've entered. (8 this summer) I hope my luck holds out next year.<P>------------------<BR>-Brian S. Fierogt321@aol.com<BR>Lincoln, NE<BR>85' SC & 87' GT's||||reg||1
Z||000002||Ed||09-30-2000||10:59 PM||||Some of us will be in a Pontiac/Oakland show here in the Sacramento, CA, area Sunday.  We'll see what happens.  <P>"She's real fine, my 409..."<P>But I did like my '64 GTO for two years until going fast, straight, got boring and I shifted over to sports cars.  ||||reg||1
