Z||000004||Phil||10-01-2000||05:56 PM||||Lar<BR>Went to a show in Brockton MA today and got put in World Compact Sports (Ricers) The rumor was that the 3rd place got like 2 votes  2nd place got 3-4 votes and 1st place got 220 votes (me). The show was run by a Camero club. heheheheheh||||reg||1
Z||000005||Ed||10-01-2000||08:38 PM||||Well, our club had seven cars in the local Pontiac show.  All Fieros there were from our local club.  But one member did win second place in semi-modified, competing against seven other Pontiacs. That seemed pretty good.  The couple has an 88 GT with T-tops, red, and nice wheels.  They show it very well.  Not much interest was generated among the goat and Trans-Am crowd, but they were hospitable. ||||reg||1
Z||000006||Phil||10-03-2000||11:08 AM||||Speaking of POCI shows, at the CT spring show we had 19-20 Fieros and at the fall show 8 Fieros. We were very well recieved. They even asked for our suggestions about breaking up the Fieros into classes. We generated a lot of interest. Very nice shows, even had free food at the fall show. It was one of the few shows that I've attended that has judging criteria printed on the ballots(nice touch).||||reg||1
